// Namespace DSL example — see .claude/commands/build-authz-service.md §5.
// Given verbatim from §5. `permission view`'s `parent->view` is a
// tuple-to-userset rule whose followed relation (`parent`) targets `folder`
// itself — self-contained, so this compiles standalone even though
// tuple-to-userset's target namespace must exist in the compilation unit
// (unlike a plain relation subject type — see document.authz's comment).
namespace folder {
  relation parent: folder
  relation editor: user | group#member

  permission view = editor | parent->view
}
